This is a bit of research for the wiki, specifically annotations for
shknam.c at

http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Shknam.c

One of the bookstore keepers is named "Kesh".  Bookstore keepers are
named for places in Eire, according to a source code comment.

Kesh is called An Cheis in Gaelic.

Kesh is apparently named either for a town or a river. The town, however,
is not in Eire as the source code claims -- it's in County Fermanagh,
Northern Ireland.  (Flames regarding the rightful ownership of the eastern
six counties of Ulster may be directed to postmaster@127.0.0.1.) But
perhaps some part of the River Kesh is in the Republic of Ireland.

Does anyone know?

